{{Quote|The Kaminoans don't create without a purpose.|[[Cut Lawquane]]|<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>}}
The '''Kaminoans''' were a tall, thin [[amphibian]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the [[Water|aquatic]] [[planet]] of [[Kamino]] in [[Wild Space]]. Living in large stilted domed cities that rose high above the ocean surface, Kaminoans were known to specialize in pioneering [[cloning]] and [[Bioengineering|genetic engineering]] technology, as well as developing more conventional, non-biomedical, technologies for various clients, [[Grand Army of the Republic|including]] the [[Galactic Republic]].

==Biology and appearance==
Kaminoans were slender, towering, pale-skinned [[humanoid]]s whose oblong heads sat atop<ref name="Episode II" /> elongated neck [[bone]]s that allowed them limited flexibility.<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> They had two large, almond-shaped [[Color|black]] [[eye]]s with white pupils<ref name="DB Kaminoan" /> that enabled them to see into the ultraviolet spectrum. [[Gender|Male]] Kaminoans had fin-like crests atop their heads, while females were completely bald and wore unique head crescents.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> Their long and frail [[limb]]s gave them a graceful, gliding walk<ref name="DB Kaminoan" /> and featured small feet adapted to their<ref name="SW:GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[homeworld]]'s firm seabeds and later hard flooring.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Kaminoans reached adulthood at 11 years old.<ref name="AEYNTK" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|You were created in our laboratories. ''You'' are Kaminoan property.|Nala Se, to clone trooper Fives|<ref name="Fugitive">{{TCW|Fugitive}}</ref>}}
[[File:TipocaCity-CC.png|thumb|left|250px|Kaminoans lived in enclosed cities above the seafloor of the planet Kamino.]]
Kaminoans generally displayed few signs of outward exuberance or personality. They considered the [[clone trooper]]s to be their finest achievement.<ref name="Episode II" /> Kaminoans were also isolationists,<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> only concerning themselves with offworlders if it was profitable.<ref name="VE" /> This traced back to the [[great flood]] that changed their homeworld of [[Kamino]], as they decided it was less risky to adapt their [[DNA|genetic code]] and [[planet]] than to ask for aid from the [[Galactic Republic]]. While the Kaminoans were able to thrive, they were left with a residual distrust when they received offers of offworld help. However, Kaminoans did not necessarily think they were superior to other species, and they instead simply saw other planets as a distraction. Many Kaminoans even thought that everything they needed was already on Kamino.<ref name="Rise" />

The Kaminoans were generally scientifically rational. However, they did often make pilgrimages to the sunken ruins of their ancient cities. Both ancient and modern Kaminoan cities were characterized by domed cities.<ref name="Complete Locations" />

==History==
===Early development===
[[File:Kamino-DB.png|thumb|right|200px|Kaminoan civilization developed on a planet that was isolated due to its location near the edge of the galaxy.]]
Hailing from the<ref name="Rise" /> planet of Kamino, located beyond the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="USW NE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> in [[Wild Space]],<ref name="EURWS">{{EncyclopediaCite|Exegol, the Unknown Regions and Wild Space}}</ref> that was considered extragalactic,<ref name="Complete Locations" /> the Kaminoans were once a land-based culture, although they still maintained a strong connection to the ocean and water, but their homeworld was at the end of a long ice age. Kamino's landforms and [[mountain]]s were unable to hold back the [[water]] from the melting ice, and this great flood forced the Kaminoans to adapt their lifestyle. The species initially moved to higher ground, but they eventually needed to build high cities to avoid the ocean. They constructed large spires and towers, which were connected to the ground that became the seafloor.<ref name="Rise" /> These towering structures replaced older wattle-and-daub structures.<ref name="Complete Locations" />

To move between the cities, Kaminoans flew on the backs of [[aiwha]]s.<ref name="VE" /> While they could have reached out to the Galactic Republic for help, the Kaminoans performed calculations and came to believe it was less risky to work on their own, as they could have been colonized, lost resources, and undergone a change in culture. The Kaminoans also preserved the land-based species and adapted themselves, their flora, and their fauna to survive on the changed planet. Their new cities were fully enclosed, which allowed the Kaminoans to survive strong winds and rainstorms, and became home to the land-bound plants and animals they were able to save.<ref name="Rise" />

===Isolation===
{{Quote|These Kaminoans keep to themselves. They're cloners. Damn good ones too.''"<br />"''Cloners. Are they friendly?''"<br />"''Depends.''"<br />"''Depends on what, Dex?''"<br />"''On how good your manners are, and how big your&hellip; pocketbook is.|Dexter Jettster educates Obi-Wan Kenobi on the pre-Clone Wars Kaminoans|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
[[File:Military_Complex.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Although they were isolated from the rest of the galaxy, Kaminoans were expert geneticists who specialized in cloning.]]
While Kamino remained unknown to most, the Kaminoan's skill in [[engineer]]ing and genetic engineering was whispered of in some parts of the underworld.<ref name="Rise" /> They also maintained a [[Bora Vio cloning facility|cloning facility]] on<ref name="Bounty Lost">{{TBB|Bounty Lost}}</ref> the world of<ref name="Bounty Lost Audio Description">Per the Audio Description for "[[Bounty Lost]]" available on [[Disney+]].</ref> [[Bora Vio]] for a [[time]], although the Kaminoans eventually abandoned it, leaving the clones created there behind.<ref name="Bounty Lost" /> [[Jedi Master]] [[Sifo-Dyas]] learned of the species and went to Kamino to order the creation of a [[Grand Army of the Republic]].<ref name="Rise" /> While they had created [[Cloning|clone]] [[Army|armies]] before,<ref name="Episode II" /> Sifo-Dyas' proposal was a bold one, but the species ultimately adapted to it and fulfilled the request.<ref name="Rise" /> However, the [[Sith]] took control of the project when [[Dooku|Darth Tyranus]] [[Currency|paid]] the [[Pyke Syndicate]] to [[Mission to Oba Diah (Sifo-Dyas)|shoot down]] Sifo-Dyas' [[T-6 shuttle]], [[Death|killing]] the [[Jedi]] Master.<ref name="The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}}</ref> Tyranus also hired [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]] to serve as the genetic template for the army. While it took ten [[Standard year|years]] for the [[troop]]s to mature, the army of clone troopers was finally ready to be introduced to the Republic.<ref name="Episode II" />

[[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] arrived on Kamino while tracking Fett, due to the [[bounty]] hunter's role in the [[plot to assassinate Senator Amidala]], and met with the Kaminoan [[Prime Minister]], [[Lama Su]], as the Kaminoans believed Kenobi had arrived to finally check on the Grand Army. Not long after the Republic learned of the army, the [[Galactic Senate]] gave [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]],<ref name="Episode II" /> who was secretly the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth]] Sidious,<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> the emergency powers needed to use the Kamino's clone army, under the guise of this power being needed to combat the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. The clone troopers saw their first deployment under their [[Jedi General]]s in the [[First Battle of Geonosis]], the first battle of the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Episode II" />

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Senator Burtoni, the Kaminoans might have bartered their creation of the clones into a seat in the Galactic Senate but this does not give you free rein.|[[Onaconda Farr]]|<ref name="Senate Murders">{{TCW|Senate Murders}}</ref>}}
[[File:Halle_Burtoni_crashes_the_party.png|thumb|right|250px|Senator Halle Burtoni represented the Kaminoans in the Galactic Senate during the Clone Wars.]]
Creating the clone army put the Kaminoans into [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]], and they also gained representation in the Republic<ref name="Rise" /> when [[Halle Burtoni]] bartered her efforts in clone production into a seat in the [[Galaxy|Galactic]] Senate.<ref name="Burtoni Databank">{{Databank|halle-burtoni|Halle Burtoni}}</ref> However, as the sole producers of the clone army, Kamino became a prime target for Confederate attack.<ref name="Rise" />

In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="SW:GA" /> the Confederacy did launch an assault on the world, but the [[Battle of Kamino]] ended in a Republic victory. After the battle, [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] believed the Separatists would not attack the planet any time soon, and [[Echo]] and [[Fives]] were promoted to [[Advanced Recon Commando|ARC troopers]]. When these clones received their promotions in one of [[Tipoca City]]'s [[hangar]]s, several Kaminoans were close by.<ref name="ARC Troopers">{{TCW|ARC Troopers (episode)}}</ref> Later in the war, Fives returned to Kamino after [[Tup]] mysteriously killed Jedi [[General]] [[Tiplar]] during the [[Battle of Ringo Vinda]].<ref name="Conspiracy">{{TCW|Conspiracy}}</ref> This was because Tup's [[behavioral modification biochip]], a secret device implanted in clones<ref name="Fugitive" /> believed to only be a defense against rogue Jedi,<ref name="Conspiracy" /> malfunctioned and caused a premature execution of [[Order 66]].<ref name="Fugitive" />

Kaminoan [[Nala Se]] tried to hide the chips from the [[Jedi Order]], but Fives was able to reveal it to Jedi Master [[Shaak Ti]].<ref name="Fugitive" /> However, Fives was [[Mission to Level 1325|eventually killed]] and failed to warn the Jedi about the true nature of the chips: they were to be used by Chancellor Palpatine to force all clones to kill their Jedi officers. Palpatine gave physical evidence of his plans, the extracted chips of Fives and Tup, to Nala Se. They were sent to Tyranus, and the Sith were now able to destroy all traces of the truth.<ref name="Orders">{{TCW|Orders (episode)}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Your people deserve to&mdash;''"<br />"''My people are gone. The few remaining Kaminoans scattered throughout the galaxy are of no importance to me, and therefore, not my concern.|Riyo Chuchi and Halle Burtoni|<ref name="Truth and Consequences">{{TBB|Truth and Consequences}}</ref>}}
[[File:Badbatch-reunion-lamasu-rampart.png|thumb|left|250px|The Galactic Empire's enlistment program threatened to replace the Kaminoans' production of clone troopers.]]
Palpatine ultimately issued Order 66 and eradicated the Jedi Order, allowing him to [[Proclamation of the New Order|transform]] the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire|First Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Episode III" /> Although the Kaminoans sought to continue their relationship with the Republic's successor, [[Admiral]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] informed Lama Su that [[Emperor]] Palpatine no longer supported their cloning production as he had during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Aftermath">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref> After learning of the Empire's [[Project War-Mantle|training program]] for [[Elite Squad Trooper|enlisted soldiers]] under [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]], Lama Su became concerned that his clones were in danger of becoming obsolete. Therefore, he believed that the future of Kaminoans hinged on providing the Empire with a new type of clone that was superior to the original Jango Fett genotype, which continued to degrade in the aftermath of the war.<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref> On Coruscant, Halle Burtoni&mdash;who suspected the Empire would turn on her people and saw Su as an arrogant individual for trying to work with the Empire<ref name="Truth and Consequences" />&mdash;lost her position in the [[Imperial Senate]] after growing too intrusive<ref name="Burtoni Databank" /> into Imperial affairs, learning that Rampart was taking Senate-approved funds for Kamino for other programs.<ref name="Truth and Consequences" />

In time, the cloning facilities on Kamino were [[Attack on Kamino|shut down]] by the Empire, which only withdrew clone troopers, clone cadets, clone embryos, material, and any Kaminoan deemed "essential," such as Nala Se.<ref name="Return to Kamino">{{TBB|Return to Kamino}}</ref> With that done, the Empire then destroyed every known Kaminoan facility<ref name="Kamino Lost">{{TBB|Kamino Lost}}</ref> and city on the planet,<ref name="Clone Conspiracy">{{TBB|The Clone Conspiracy}}</ref> including Tipoca City. Members of the Kaminoan population had been forcibly interned and deported prior<ref name="RiseAndFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> or were caught in the attacks, killing them. Overall, only a small number of survivors were scattered across the stars.<ref name="Truth and Consequences" /> The Empire then withdrew from Kamino, focusing its [[Imperial cloning program|future cloning operations]] within [[Mount Tantiss]] on [[Wayland]]. Pressed into Imperial service, Se was brought to the facility to help with its projects.<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> In part through the efforts of a reluctant to help Burtoni, the truth of Kamino's destruction was revealed by Senator [[Riyo Chuchi]], but Palpatine blamed the attack on Rampart and his clones alone, using it to help push through the [[Imperial Defense Recruitment Bill]].<ref name="Truth and Consequences" />

Later in the Imperial Era, the [[pirate]] [[Hondo Ohnaka]] noted that he saw fewer Kaminoans in the galaxy.<ref name="Pirate's Price">''[[Pirate's Price]]''</ref> Some Kaminoans went on to join the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], but the amorality they showed in medical matters, combined with the role they had played in the rise of the Empire, created a difficult relationship between them and their fellow Rebels.<ref name="Fully Operational">[[Fully Operational (sourcebook)|''Fully Operational'']]</ref> With the Empire having claimed the Kaminoan cloning technology<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> and secured a monopoly over its use,<ref name="Metamorphosis">{{TBB|Metamorphosis (episode)}}</ref> Sidious's [[Sith Eternal]] cult<ref name="SotS">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref> used Kaminoan cloning technology<ref name="Family at War">''[[Skywalker: A Family at War]]''</ref> and [[Strand-Cast]]ing in an effort to create cloned bodies for Palpatine, thereby ensuring he could pass his spirit into a new form if he died<ref name="SotS" /> and rule forever.<ref name="Family at War" />

==Kaminoans in the galaxy==
During the [[High Republic Era]], one such Kaminoan walked the streets of [[Bri-Phrang City]] on [[Eriadu]] when the planet was trapped inside the [[Occlusion Zone]].<ref name="DftOZ 1">[[The High Republic Adventures – Dispatches from the Occlusion Zone 1|''The High Republic Adventures – Dispatches from the Occlusion Zone'' 1]]</ref>

One of the clones kept in the abandoned cloning facility on Bora Vio was a Kaminoan.<ref name="Bounty Lost" />

The Kaminoan [[Kan Be]] was a [[crime lord]] during the [[Cold War]] between the [[First Order]] and [[New Republic]]. He joined forces with [[First Order Security Bureau]] [[agent]] [[Terex]] during the [[mission to Megalox Beta]].<ref name="Poe Dameron 5">[[Poe Dameron 5|''Poe Dameron'' 5]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The design of the Kaminoans was inspired by the aliens from [[Steven Spielberg]]'s film ''Close Encounters of the Third Kind'', which were themselves based on the "grey alien" of folklore.<ref name="100 Scenes">''[[Star Wars in 100 Scenes]]''</ref>

